s printed as closest hundreds, closest tens or closest thousands, which is awkward for nearest hundred but not wrong; F07 says the number is marked on the number line, and the packet shows no number-line field, so I could not verify it; and every printed number lacks the space separator the vocabulary block declares (for example 1005 rather than 1 005). The number format is a declared ground truth, but it is not a Rule 1 failure category. F01, F02, F03, F04, F06, F07, F08 and F09 pass on the templates and domains shown. The declared domains and printed runs show no value that makes any of them wrong for a grade 3 Q1 learner.\"}",
